{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat docs/evidence/rust-rewrite/final-audit-20260913.md; cat docs/evidence/rust-rewrite/ci-gates-audit-20260913.md; sed -n '1,260p' hugegraph-store/rust/store-core/src/lib.rs\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat docs/evidence/rust-rewrite/final-audit-20260913.md; cat docs/evidence/rust-rewrite/ci-gates-audit-20260913.md; sed -n '1,260p' hugegraph-store/rust/store-core/src/lib.rs\"","aggregated_output":"# Rust 重写阶段审计记录\n\n- Contract matrix: 6/6 complete; independent oracles and mutation validation archived.\n- Differential replay: baseline and selector switch/rollback trace pass; evidence `differential-replay-20260913.log`, `differential-switch-rollback-20260913.log`.\n- Fault recovery: restart recovery and corrupted snapshot rejection pass (`fault-recovery-20260913.log`).\n- Performance/resource: release timing and max RSS captured (`store-performance-resource-20260913.log`).\n- CI gates: fmt, clippy, locked debug/release tests pass (`production-ci-gates-20260913.log`).\n- Audit decision: **NO-GO**. Production integration and maintainer/reviewer sign-offs are not yet evidenced. Java fallback remains caller-selectable for rollback.\n# CI gate audit (2026-09-13)\n\nCommand: `tools/rust-partition-poc/audit-gates.sh`\n\nExit code: 0. The script inspected `.github/workflows/rust-partition-poc.yml` and confirmed the workflow executes all four local POC gates: `cargo fmt -- --check`, clippy with `-D warnings`, `cargo test --locked`, and `cargo mutants --exclude src/main.rs --timeout 30 --jobs 2`.\n\nThis is evidence that the declared POC gates are wired into CI. It does not establish production Rust coverage, Java/Rust differential compatibility, or end-to-end snapshot/restart coverage; those remain MISSING in the acceptance matrix.\n//! Independent Rust store boundary. Java remains selectable by the caller.\n\npub trait StoreBackend {\n    fn put(&mut self, key: Vec<u8>, value: Vec<u8>) -> Option<Vec<u8>>;\n    fn get(&self, key: &[u8]) -> Option<Vec<u8>>;\n    fn rollback(&mut self, key: &[u8]);\n}\n\n#[derive(Default)]\npub struct InMemoryStore(std::collections::BTreeMap<Vec<u8>, Vec<u8>>);\n\nimpl InMemoryStore {\n    pub fn snapshot(&self) -> Vec<u8> {\n        self.0\n            .iter()\n            .flat_map(|(k, v)| {\n                [k.len() as u32]\n                    .into_iter()\n                    .flat_map(|n| n.to_le_bytes())\n                    .chain(k.iter().copied())\n                    .chain([v.len() as u32].into_iter().flat_map(|n| n.to_le_bytes()))\n                    .chain(v.iter().copied())\n            })\n            .collect()\n    }\n    pub fn restore(bytes: &[u8]) -> Option<Self> {\n        let mut p = 0;\n        let mut m = std::collections::BTreeMap::new();\n        while p < bytes.len() {\n            if p + 4 > bytes.len() {\n                return None;\n            };\n            let kl = u32::from_le_bytes(bytes[p..p + 4].try_into().ok()?) as usize;\n            p += 4;\n            if p + kl + 4 > bytes.len() {\n                return None;\n            };\n            let k = bytes[p..p + kl].to_vec();\n            p += kl;\n            let vl = u32::from_le_bytes(bytes[p..p + 4].try_into().ok()?) as usize;\n            p += 4;\n            if p + vl > bytes.len() {\n                return None;\n            };\n            m.insert(k, bytes[p..p + vl].to_vec());\n            p += vl;\n        }\n        Some(Self(m))\n    }\n}\n\npub enum BackendSelector {\n    Rust(InMemoryStore),\n    JavaFallback(InMemoryStore),\n}\n\nimpl BackendSelector {\n    pub fn rust() -> Self {\n        Self::Rust(InMemoryStore::default())\n    }\n    pub fn java_fallback() -> Self {\n        Self::JavaFallback(InMemoryStore::default())\n    }\n    pub fn switch_to_java(self) -> Self {\n        Self::JavaFallback(match self {\n            Self::Rust(s) | Self::JavaFallback(s) => s,\n        })\n    }\n    pub fn switch_to_rust(self) -> Self {\n        Self::Rust(match self {\n            Self::Rust(s) | Self::JavaFallback(s) => s,\n        })\n    }\n}\n\nimpl StoreBackend for BackendSelector {\n    fn put(&mut self, key: Vec<u8>, value: Vec<u8>) -> Option<Vec<u8>> {\n        match self {\n            Self::Rust(s) | Self::JavaFallback(s) => s.put(key, value),\n        }\n    }\n    fn get(&self, key: &[u8]) -> Option<Vec<u8>> {\n        match self {\n            Self::Rust(s) | Self::JavaFallback(s) => s.get(key),\n        }\n    }\n    fn rollback(&mut self, key: &[u8]) {\n        match self {\n            Self::Rust(s) | Self::JavaFallback(s) => s.rollback(key),\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nimpl StoreBackend for InMemoryStore {\n    fn put(&mut self, key: Vec<u8>, value: Vec<u8>) -> Option<Vec<u8>> {\n        self.0.insert(key, value)\n    }\n    fn get(&self, key: &[u8]) -> Option<Vec<u8>> {\n        self.0.get(key).cloned()\n    }\n    fn rollback(&mut self, key: &[u8]) {\n        self.0.remove(key);\n    }\n}\n\n#[cfg(test)]\nmod tests {\n    use super::*;\n    #[test]\n    fn commit_and_rollback_visibility() {\n        let mut s = InMemoryStore::default();\n        assert_eq!(s.put(b\"k\".to_vec(), b\"v\".to_vec()), None);\n        assert_eq!(s.get(b\"k\"), Some(b\"v\".to_vec()));\n        s.rollback(b\"k\");\n        assert_eq!(s.get(b\"k\"), None);\n    }\n    #[test]\n    fn selectable_java_fallback_rollback() {\n        let mut b = BackendSelector::rust();\n        b.put(b\"k\".to_vec(), b\"v\".to_vec());\n        b = b.switch_to_java();\n        assert_eq!(b.get(b\"k\"), Some(b\"v\".to_vec()));\n        b.rollback(b\"k\");\n        b = b.switch_to_rust();\n        assert_eq!(b.get(b\"k\"), None);\n    }\n\n    #[test]\n    fn restart_recovery_and_corruption_rejection() {\n        let mut s = InMemoryStore::default();\n        s.put(b\"a\".to_vec(), b\"1\".to_vec());\n        s.put(b\"b\".to_vec(), b\"2\".to_vec());\n        let image = s.snapshot();\n        let recovered = InMemoryStore::restore(&image).unwrap();\n        assert_eq!(recovered.get(b\"a\"), Some(b\"1\".to_vec()));\n        assert_eq!(recovered.get(b\"b\"), Some(b\"2\".to_vec()));\n        let mut corrupt = image.clone();\n        corrupt.pop();\n        assert!(InMemoryStore::restore(&corrupt).is_none());\n    }\n    #[test]\n    fn snapshot_round_trip() {\n        let mut s = InMemoryStore::default();\n        s.put(b\"k\".to_vec(), b\"v\".to_vec());\n        let r = InMemoryStore::restore(&s.snapshot()).unwrap();\n        assert_eq!(r.get(b\"k\"), Some(b\"v\".to_vec()));\n    }\n\n    #[test]\n    fn differential_switch_rollback_trace() {\n        fn run(mut b: BackendSelector) -> Vec<Option<Vec<u8>>> {\n            let mut out = Vec::new();\n            out.push(b.put(b\"a\".to_vec(), b\"1\".to_vec()));\n            out.push(b.get(b\"a\"));\n            b = b.switch_to_java();\n            out.push(b.put(b\"b\".to_vec(), b\"2\".to_vec()));\n            out.push(b.get(b\"a\"));\n            b.rollback(b\"a\");\n            b = b.switch_to_rust();\n            out.push(b.get(b\"a\"));\n            out.push(b.get(b\"b\"));\n            out\n        }\n        assert_eq!(run(BackendSelector::rust()), run(BackendSelector::java_fallback()));\n    }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
